    config KILNCTL_LOG_TEE_CONSOLE
        bool "Also print log lines to the console UART"
        default y
        help
            uart_log_bridge replaces console logging with a push to the PC
            link. That queue drops lines when full, which it reliably is
            during the boot burst -- so the board's own account of a failed
            bring-up is exactly what gets lost. With this on, every line also
            goes to the console UART (GPIO43/44), where nothing can drop it.

            Costs a blocking console write per log line. Turn it off if a
            logging-heavy path ever needs the microseconds back.

    menu "Simulated plant (development only)"

        config KILNCTL_SIM_PLANT
            bool "Run the control stack against a simulated kiln"
            default n
            help
                Feeds the profile executor, autotune engine, and dashboard
                from App/test/sim_plant.c's thermal model instead of the
                MAX31856 thermocouples, and lets faults (dead element,
                welded relay, detached/frozen/open thermocouple) be injected
                over POST /api/sim. This is how the thermal guards get
                exercised end to end without a kiln -- and without the
                thermocouple daughterboard or relay expander, neither of
                which is attached to the bench unit.

                LEAVE THIS OFF FOR ANYTHING THAT WILL BE NEAR A REAL KILN.
                With it on the board reports fabricated temperatures and
                will happily claim a healthy firing with nothing plugged in.
                Relay writes still go out to the real expander if one is
                present, so a sim build must not be flashed to a board wired
                to elements.

        config KILNCTL_SIM_AMBIENT_C
            int "Simulated ambient temperature (degC)"
            depends on KILNCTL_SIM_PLANT
            default 20

        config KILNCTL_SIM_THERMAL_MASS_J_PER_C
            int "Simulated zone thermal mass (J per degC)"
            depends on KILNCTL_SIM_PLANT
            default 50000
            help
                With the default loss coefficient this sets the zone's time
                constant tau = mass/loss = 10000s, which is kiln-like.

        config KILNCTL_SIM_HEATER_POWER_W
            int "Simulated element power per zone (W, at duty 1.0)"
            depends on KILNCTL_SIM_PLANT
            default 2000

        config KILNCTL_SIM_LOSS_W_PER_C
            int "Simulated linear heat loss (W per degC above ambient)"
            depends on KILNCTL_SIM_PLANT
            default 5
            help
                Sets the duty-1.0 ceiling: ambient + power/loss (420 degC
                with the defaults here). Raise the power or lower this to
                simulate a kiln that can reach cone temperature.

        config KILNCTL_SIM_RADIATIVE_COEFF_E12
            int "Simulated radiative loss coefficient (units of 1e-12 W per K^4)"
            depends on KILNCTL_SIM_PLANT
            default 2000
            help
                Adds a Stefan-Boltzmann loss term on top of the linear one,
                so plant gain falls with temperature the way a real kiln's
                does. 0 disables it (purely linear plant). Expressed in
                1e-12 units because Kconfig has no float type; the default
                2000 means 2e-9 W/K^4.

        config KILNCTL_SIM_COUPLING_W_PER_C
            int "Simulated inter-zone conductance (W per degC)"
            depends on KILNCTL_SIM_PLANT
            default 3
            help
                How strongly each zone heats its neighbors. 0 makes the
                zones independent, which is the one thing a real
                multi-zone kiln is not.

        config KILNCTL_SIM_SENSOR_DELAY_S
            int "Simulated sensor transport delay (s)"
            depends on KILNCTL_SIM_PLANT
            default 5

        config KILNCTL_SIM_SENSOR_LAG_S
            int "Simulated thermocouple lag time constant (s)"
            depends on KILNCTL_SIM_PLANT
            default 8

        config KILNCTL_SIM_SENSOR_NOISE_MC
            int "Simulated sensor noise, peak-to-peak (milli-degC)"
            depends on KILNCTL_SIM_PLANT
            default 0
            help
                0 for a clean reading. 1000 (i.e. 1 degC) is a reasonable
                value for checking that the guards do not false-trip on
                noise alone.

    endmenu

    config KILNCTL_HEARTBEAT_LED_GPIO
        int "Heartbeat LED GPIO (-1 to disable)"
        default -1
        range -1 48
        help
            The main board has no MCU-driven LED -- D25/D28 are rail
            indicators tied straight to 3.3V/5V -- and the dev board's
            addressable RGB LED is removed on this build. Left at -1 the
            monitor task still runs and still reports over the log link; it
            just doesn't blink anything.

    config KILNCTL_ENABLE_GPIO_PROBE
        bool "Enable raw GPIO probe over UART (debug only)"
        default n
        help
            Adds UART_TASK_ID_GPIO_PROBE: set-mode/write/read on ESP32-S3
            pins from the PC, gated by a hard deny-list (SPI, I2C, the
            SX1509 IRQ/RESET pins, the display CS, the PC-link UART pins,
            and every safety-link pin including GPIO6/SAFETY_FAULT_IO) and
            refused outright while a profile is running. Exists to answer
            "is this net where the schematic says" without a one-off
            firmware -- tools/PcTools/TODO.md capability 1.

            Leave this OFF for any build going near a real heater. It is a
            bench/bring-up tool, not a production capability: a debug tool
            that can twiddle arbitrary pins on a board that drives mains
            relays is exactly the hazard docs/SAFETY_MODEL.md exists to
            avoid, and the deny-list is enforced in this firmware, not by
            whoever is holding the PC end.

endmenu
